KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the yielded value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ and clang++ (GCC 16 for C++23 and C++26) accept this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  Coroutines are parsed but not implemented; see
cpp20_coroutine_generator_semantics for what CBMC does instead and what a fix
needs.

Since coroutines are reported as unsupported, the call of the coroutine
also fails the property "coroutines are not supported" and ends the path.
